IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `rra-nouns`
IMPORT `rra-seat`

-- Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993 -- WORKED CASES for the seat layer.
-- One employee throughout: born on 1 January 1960, with a prescribed minimum retirement age of 63 (so the specified age is
-- attained on 1 January 2023), a prescribed re-employment age of 68 (attained on 1 January 2028), and no retirement age
-- stipulated in the contract unless a case says so.  Every expected value is written from the text of the section named
-- beside the case, before the assertion was run.

§ `Cases -- my age and the retirement ages (ss 2 and 4)`

-- s 2(3): the anniversary of the date of birth.
#ASSERT `On what date do I attain the prescribed minimum retirement age` (Date 1 1 1960) 63 EQUALS JUST (Date 1 1 2023)
-- Born on 29 February: 2023 has no 29 February and the Act does not say which date stands in; 2024 does.
#ASSERT `On what date do I attain the prescribed minimum retirement age` (Date 29 2 1960) 63 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `On what date do I attain the prescribed minimum retirement age` (Date 29 2 1960) 64 EQUALS JUST (Date 29 2 2024)
-- Age not known (0): not answered.
#ASSERT `On what date do I attain the prescribed minimum retirement age` (Date 1 1 1960) 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 2(1) "specified age": the higher of the prescribed minimum retirement age and the contract's age.
#ASSERT `On what date do I attain my specified age` (Date 1 1 1960) 63 0 EQUALS JUST (Date 1 1 2023)
#ASSERT `On what date do I attain my specified age` (Date 1 1 1960) 63 65 EQUALS JUST (Date 1 1 2025)
#ASSERT `On what date do I attain my specified age` (Date 1 1 1960) 63 60 EQUALS JUST (Date 1 1 2023)
#ASSERT `On what date do I attain my specified age` (Date 1 1 1960) 0 65 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Have I attained my specified age` (Date 1 1 1960) 63 0 (Date 1 1 2023) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Have I attained my specified age` (Date 1 1 1960) 63 0 (Date 31 12 2022) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Have I attained my specified age` (Date 1 1 1960) 63 65 (Date 1 1 2023) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Have I attained my specified age` (Date 1 1 1960) 0 0 (Date 1 1 2023) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 2(2): treated as dismissed
#ASSERT `Am I treated as dismissed` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I treated as dismissed` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I treated as dismissed` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I treated as dismissed` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 4(2): the day before the prescribed minimum retirement age the Act says no; on the day itself it is silent.
#ASSERT `May my employer dismiss me on the ground of age` (Date 1 1 1960) 63 TRUE (Date 31 12 2022) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May my employer dismiss me on the ground of age` (Date 1 1 1960) 63 TRUE (Date 31 12 2022) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May my employer dismiss me on the ground of age` (Date 1 1 1960) 63 TRUE (Date 1 1 2023) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `May my employer dismiss me on the ground of age` (Date 1 1 1960) 63 FALSE (Date 31 12 2022) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `May my employer dismiss me on the ground of age` (Date 1 1 1960) 0 TRUE (Date 31 12 2022) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 4(1): at least 62, not more than 65, by notification in the Gazette
#ASSERT `Can this age be the prescribed minimum retirement age` 63 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can this age be the prescribed minimum retirement age` 66 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can this age be the prescribed minimum retirement age` 63 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 4(3)
#ASSERT `Is my employer guilty of an offence for dismissing me early` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my employer guilty of an offence for dismissing me early` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 6: a term below 63 is void; a term at 63 or above is not touched by this section
#ASSERT `Is the retirement age in my contract void` 63 TRUE 62 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the retirement age in my contract void` 63 TRUE 63 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is the retirement age in my contract void` 63 FALSE 62 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `What retirement age does the term leave standing` 63 62 EQUALS 63
#ASSERT `What retirement age does the term leave standing` 63 65 EQUALS 65

§ `Cases -- am I eligible for re-employment (s 7)`

#ASSERT `Am I eligible for re-employment` (Date 1 1 1960) Yes FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for re-employment` (Date 30 6 1952) Yes FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for re-employment` (Date 1 1 1960) No FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for re-employment` (Date 1 1 1960) Yes TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The employer's assessment is not known and nothing else fails: the Act does not answer.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for re-employment` (Date 1 1 1960) `I am not sure` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Am I presumed medically fit` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I presumed medically fit` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Has my employer given me the notice it owed` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Has my employer given me the notice it owed` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Has my employer given me the notice it owed` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Has my employer given me the notice it owed` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Cases -- must I be offered re-employment, when, and on what terms (s 7A)`

-- s 7A(1): subject to s 7C
#ASSERT `Does my employer owe me an offer of re-employment` Yes No EQUALS JUST TRUE
